  "title": "ArcFarms mine events and workshop throughput economy 2026-10-23",
  "assumptions": [
    "Comparison is current live ArcFarms .49 vs the proposed event-pool/workshop revision; it is not the earlier pre-.49 payout change.",
    "Sensitivity only: active hours/player-day [0.25, 1, 2]; cycles/hour before [3, 6, 10], after [3.2, 6.5, 11]. Assumed completions/day are their products: before [0.75, 6, 20], after [0.8, 6.5, 22]. These are not telemetry or guarantees.",
    "Participants [5, 10, 20] are active eligible contributors in the low/base/high network scenarios. The full mine-completion reward is granted to each positive contributor; no group splitting is assumed.",
    "Four orders rotate equally over the long run. Their current .49 per-completion direct payouts average 274.5 Vault and 411.75 vanilla XP; same before and after. Bundle item EV is also unchanged per completion and uses integer-floor scaling before weighting.",
    "Crystal Resonance adds at most 4 shared zone-order progress credits once when that incident resolves. It is not a player-inventory item or currency, and adds no Vault, tokens, vanilla XP, physical drops, SELL or contract redemption. Its frequency is not assumed.",
    "Current live .49 config and active 11-type pool were verified by the parent; CRYSTAL_RESONANCE is force-only there. Candidate pool is 14 types (old 11 plus CRYSTAL_RESONANCE, FREIGHT_WINCH and DRAINAGE_PUMP), still one scheduled incident per cycle. No 1/14 frequency is inferred.",
    "The workshop sensitivity is supplied as an assumption: an automatic batch takes 4s crush + 3s transfer + 6s heat + 5s pour = 18s; 3 batches are 54s and 2 are 36s. Existing accepted 18-credit work retains 3 batches; newly accepted 12-credit work uses 2.",
    "Savings retain 80% of direct mine Vault as in the earlier assessment. This expense allowance is not measured and is not modeled as a burn.",
    "Existing bundle SELL and contract amounts below are alternative all-units-converted sensitivities from the earlier assessment, not direct mine rewards. The same item cannot be sold through both routes; actual dynamic prices, acceptance, individual caps and available contract budget can reduce them."
  ],
